{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "4688fb15-177e-8661-a454-cc54ff83b4a4",
  "created_at": "2026-02-23T14:02:22-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Alan Chase",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:22-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:25-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, Kevin. Yes. This is Alan Chase. I'm calling about... well, about water. In my cellar."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:32-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Mr. Chase. Water in the cellar. Was this from the storm over the weekend?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:38-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That nor'easter, Saturday into Sunday. [pause] A few inches came up through the floor. Seeped in, really. Sunday morning I went down and it was just sitting there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:49-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Gotcha. Few inches, Sunday morning. Has that happened at your place before?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:59:54-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. Never. I've been in this house, oh, a good many years and the cellar has always been dry. [pause] That's what gets me. Never once."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:04-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so first time. Writing that down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:08-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It wasn't this bad last winter. We had snow, we had rain, and nothing. So something's changed out there. [pause] I'm sorry, I lost my place. The drain. The one in the street, it was just full, running over. Nobody's cleaned it, I'd bet on that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:25-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the storm drain out front, you're saying, it was overflowing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:30-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that one. And I'd like to know, is that a city drain or a state one? Because I've heard it can be either, and I don't want to be sent around in circles."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:43-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair question. It depends on the road. If it's a city street, it's ours. If it's a state road, it belongs to the state. Can you give me the street you're on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:00:55-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. [pause] I'd rather not go into that just now. I only wanted to know who it belongs to."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:01:03-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, no problem. I can't say for certain without the street, but most of the neighborhood streets are city. If you call back with the location, or give it to me now, I can put in a request for a crew to look at the drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:01:20-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. [pause] Well. I keep thinking somebody should have been out checking these before a storm like that. It's a lot of water to have in a business building and nobody even looked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:01:33-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Crews are stretched thin after a storm like that, they work through a list. Is the water still down there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:01:42-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Most of it's gone. I've been mopping, and wiping down the counters upstairs, they got damp too. [pause] Listen to that cloth squeak. It's the dampness, I think."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:01:53-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I hear it. Okay, here's what I've got: cellar seepage Sunday, first time, drain out front overflowing. I'll note you asked about city versus state."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:02:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. And, um... what was the other thing. [pause] Yes. Will somebody call me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:02:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can have someone call. What's a good number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:02:13-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0182."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:02:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0182. We'll be in touch, Mr. Chase."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T14:02:19-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "All right. Thank you, Kevin."
    }
  ],
